  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`.\n\nThe requirement says the skill must open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. The file has a title and a two-sentence intro paragraph. The first section, `## Workflow`, comes right after them. Its steps are a numbered checklist, `- [ ] 1.` through `- [ ] 7.`, so they are ordered steps. The sections \"Writing chapters\", \"Choosing references\", \"What the review checks\" and \"Gotchas\" all come after the workflow.\n\nThe intro paragraph sits under the H1 title and is not a separate section, so I do not count it as another section before the workflow. A stricter reading could object to it, but the wording does not support that reading as well as it supports mine.\n\nThe site's query listed no violation matches to judge. I found no gap.",
